{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Hansen moved to dismiss the clause (iv) charges on First Amendment overbreadth grounds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e43440bd8c86-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas asked whether the statute had ever been applied in the way the Ninth Circuit hypothesized."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e43440bd8c8668b44b73d6a5ccfe1c4c3592903ee3965a202f339cf9604bae15",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e43440bd8c86-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned how the Court could strike down one part of the statute while preserving another."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background & Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2022-22-179",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that clause (iv) uses \u201cencourages or induces\u201d in its specialized, criminal\u2011law sense, incorporating common\u2011law liability for solicitation and facilitation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court further held that to the extent clause (iv) reaches any speech, it stretches no further than speech integral to unlawful conduct."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas (concurring) warned that the facial overbreadth doctrine allows courts to strike down laws in the abstract without any concrete application."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson (dissenting) emphasized that the statute\u2019s purpose is to prohibit encouragement or inducement of non\u2011citizens to unlawfully enter, remain, or reside in the United States."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), Congress's removal of \u201cwillfully or knowingly\u201d in the 1986 amendments did not change the mens\u2011rea required to violate this statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), the 1986 amendment added \u201creside\u201d to the prohibited conduct."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), aiding\u2011and\u2011abetting liability is a centuries\u2011old principle allowing responsibility for crimes one did not personally commit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), punishment for the encouragement provision is not tied to the punishment for the underlying offense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), the majority has mounted a serious invasion of the legislative domain."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 49,
              "start": 49
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), the majority downplays the encouragement provision's threat to free expression by highlighting that Hansen fails to identify a single prosecution for protected expression in the 70 years since Congress enacted clause (iv)'s predecessor."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0004-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson (dissenting), the Government now seeks to read into the statute the very element it previously opposed as a textual limitation."
      }
    ],
