              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Helaman Hansen, united States v. Hansen concerned the meaning of clause (iv) of a criminal statute that makes it illegal to encourage or induce non\u2011citizens to reside in the United States unlawfully."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-da6d7c826c76-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the terms \u201cencourages\u201d and \u201cinduces\u201d are to be read in their specialized criminal\u2011law sense, limiting the statute to speech that is integral to unlawful conduct."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
