              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6d7c826c76-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 2,
                "start": 2
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Helaman Hansen, Hansen argues that clause (iv) punishes so much protected speech that it cannot be applied to anyone, including himself."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Helaman Hansen",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6d7c826c76-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Helaman Hansen, he contends that clause (iv) uses \u201cencourages\u201d and \u201cinduces\u201d in their ordinary sense, not a specialized criminal meaning."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Hansen",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "da6d7c826c762aa78dc8297cd23f41573001ad199e2db1c6ae55605cc41f1687",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-da6d7c826c76-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 15,
                "start": 14
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Hansen, he further argues that the ordinary meanings include aiding and abetting, so the statute would prohibit even an op\u2011ed criticizing immigration if the audience includes undocumented persons."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Helaman Hansen",
      "status": "complete",
